{"id": "EUVD-2026-108777", "enisaUuid": "ef816773-56cf-3e88-91ff-d4c905c75126", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nunshare: don't drop active namespace references that were never taken\n\nActive references on the namespaces of an nsproxy are taken when the\nnsproxy is installed into a task in switch_task_namespaces() and\ncopy_namespaces() and dropped again by put_nsproxy() through\ndeactivate_nsproxy().\n\nBut ksys_unshare() calls put_nsproxy() on an nsproxy that was never\ninstalled when set_cred_ucounts() fails. The new namespaces of that\nnsproxy go from zero to minus one and the namespaces shared with the\ncaller lose a reference that belongs to the nsproxy the caller keeps\nusing:\n\n  WARNING: kernel/nscommon.c:171 at __ns_ref_active_put+0x1cd/0x230\n   nsproxy_ns_active_put\n   deactivate_nsproxy\n   ksys_unshare\n\nAfterwards the namespaces the caller lives in aren't listed by listns()\nanymore. set_cred_ucounts() only fails when alloc_ucounts() can't\nallocate and it only allocates when the real uid of the caller differs\nfrom its effective uid.\n\nCommit cefd55bd2159 (\"nsproxy: fix free_nsproxy() and simplify\ncreate_new_namespaces()\") separated the two cases on purpose.\nnsproxy_free() frees an nsproxy that was prepared but never installed\nand that's what a failed setns() uses in put_nsset(). Export it and use\nit for a failed unshare() as well.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:20:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:20:00", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56fe03a0c05dba4c5f6a23c391f96de1614a098c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b6f31a3c0b16066f812e94b52a704174a6f23cd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98983"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06350e02-51eb-36b2-aab8-da56b128ffd4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.33 <6.19"}, {"id": "185c867f-c258-3348-b5dd-5d6abc2e702b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.175 <6.2"}, {"id": "19cbf069-62ec-39cd-9532-23a786d0ea2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "813a47b0309097da71781ee4ac11922e39b67d55"}, {"id": "1c587a75-6362-3feb-9166-cacbc92bfea2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "27565171-04b7-33ae-86e4-14fd82f21030", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6e608e3e5ce12ce7fd21e46212eccca37f917d0e"}, {"id": "4e6cdc49-926c-3671-b877-8b9a5bfa730a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27ae6b17c9ba7ff353ab0906297f08aa845782b4"}, {"id": "54491982-b189-336c-8707-262be5a3455d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5900d601-2587-3778-8eb0-e3851761adf4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.141 <6.7"}, {"id": "751a4bd6-d394-3eb9-962c-b0688e58f7dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a98621a0f187a934c115dcfe79a49520ae892111 <56fe03a0c05dba4c5f6a23c391f96de1614a098c"}, {"id": "8124b5ac-9e37-32a2-ac28-447bff800f56", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a261fccdb4ac58ec5ba6aa1d92a6cc418fff301f"}, {"id": "9545b062-9d4e-31f1-acf2-de7ed63c5aca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "665dc1ed16357988d439fc5bbc860ee36f540d81"}, {"id": "9878f486-19b6-3734-87c3-7869567fdecd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "297261b343371c4f0b31055d53d285138ec21565"}, {"id": "ad73eb6f-fcab-3a94-9331-4c6a0d3b7cca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.209 <5.16"}, {"id": "b1203591-daeb-316d-a16d-3a591812c598", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0.10 <7.1"}, {"id": "bc0f1885-95c7-3c4c-84be-81bba275ace7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a98621a0f187a934c115dcfe79a49520ae892111 <0b6f31a3c0b16066f812e94b52a704174a6f23cd"}, {"id": "d76b1605-f9c2-3dec-8957-06bf5683be3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.91 <6.13"}, {"id": "f2964dd9-4d65-3bf3-a56b-5906f8b64146", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "f741b510-33fc-3bfe-a91d-ec6b42bd08f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "97dbe0bb-8e1a-34f5-a16b-7eeb0c66f949", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}